WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.419
It was courtside,
sitting next to him.

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:05.338
I can't remember what game it was, but,

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.216
but my experience is kind of the opposite.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:10.844
He's so locked in. He doesn't break.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.430
So, like, saying what's
up to him in warm-up lines,

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.432
all that good stuff was cool.

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:19.019
But then when the game was
on, sitting, like,

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.146
two seats away from
him, you know what I mean?

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:26.317
It's just kinda like how focused
he is on what he's in the

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:28.528
middle of and what he's doing.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.739
Even when you try to get,
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.283
Like, you know, “Hey, I’m still sitting here.
Same guy

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.784
you said what's up to.
Like, we know each other.

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:38.246
We actually worked together.”
- Like, talk to me.
- Nothing? OK, cool.

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:40.373
It's like you respect the workplace,

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.207
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:44.252
And the drive of like of what
mission he's out on right now.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:46.046
So that was just like, you know,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.757
the opposite of how—
not the opposite, but just,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:51.926
he just was so locked in.

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:55.263
It was, it was, you know,
always impressive.

